agent-tools (1.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * claude-sync: stop when a session record can't be read, instead of
    treating that session as closed and syncing it while it runs.
  * claude-sync: stop when a file or directory can't be scanned, instead of
    treating it as deleted.
  * claude-sync: save the sync base on the peer before saving it locally, so
    a failed push can't make a later edit on the peer look unchanged.
  * claude-sync: chain diverged transcripts onto the leaf --resume continues
    from, put a compacted tail first, split on newlines only, and make
    re-merging idempotent.
  * claude-sync: merge history.jsonl and MEMORY.md on newlines only; a prompt
    containing U+2028 was split in two and corrupted the history on both
    machines.
  * claude-sync: refuse machine ids that could be paths, give each trash
    operation its own directory, don't purge trash on a dry run, and make
    rsync copy every file it is given.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:54:58 -0700

agent-tools (1.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * claude-sync: write merged transcripts, conflict copies and its own state
    owner-only (0600); they were created with the umask and could be read by
    other users.
  * claude-sync: refuse file paths from the peer that would leave ~/.claude,
    and never copy symlinks.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:57:49 -0700

agent-tools (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * claude-sync: new tool. Two-way sync of Claude Code sessions between two
    machines over ssh and rsync, so a session can be resumed on either one.
    A session continued on both machines is chained into one conversation,
    with both originals kept as conflict copies.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:49:36 -0700

agent-tools (1.0.1) unstable; urgency=low

  * agent-ps: keep INFO on one row and cut it to the terminal width; a prompt
    passed in argv no longer spills across the table. Add --wide to disable.

